From a2a97c70c0bf87243308e2e225e6202c9122f694 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:22:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dispatch): filter pickup dropdown to Fship-registered
 addresses for Fship shipments

The Dispatch page's pickup dropdown listed every Shiprocket/Bigship pickup
location alongside the handful of addresses actually registered with Fship
(Settings > Carrier Config > Fship > Additional Pickup Addresses). Picking
one of the non-Fship entries for an Fship shipment always fell back to the
Fship default -- correct given no Fship address id exists for those, but
there was no way to tell which entries were actually usable before booking,
which is how "rareprint office" (never added to Fship) got picked and
silently reverted, right after confirming the resolveWarehouse() precedence
fix (2187f51) works correctly for addresses that ARE registered.

Filters the dropdown to Fship-only entries whenever a shipment is
effectively going via Fship (explicit "Ship via: Fship", or "Default" while
Fship is the globally active carrier -- fetched from GET /carrier-config).
Switching carrier now also clears any stale pickup selection. Bigship/
Shiprocket selection is unchanged; "compare" mode is left unfiltered since
it quotes both Bigship and Fship together.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0113oeqpEZauy9eX9fYyMYhZ
